# Friends — game design

Product: [docs/product.md](../../docs/product.md). Strategy: [docs/strategy.md](../../docs/strategy.md). Roadmap: [docs/roadmap.md](../../docs/roadmap.md). Skill: [friends-game-design](../skills/friends-game-design/SKILL.md).

## MUST

- Room key = Discord Activity `instanceId` (unique). First joiner sets `hostUserId` for DB only — **no host powers** in the Activity.
- **A-only MVP:** API serves **`most_likely` only** (unused prompt for room locale). No category picker / pack filter.
- Do **not** add a second equal in-Activity mode (async quiz / “make your quiz” / daily) until [roadmap.md](../../docs/roadmap.md) Phase 5 unlock + product says so.
- Schema may still list `this_or_that` | `truth` | `challenge` and legacy `PromptCategory` — not in the default start loop.
- Do not reveal `most_likely` / `truth` answers or running scores to clients mid-session — public DTO masks them until `finished`.
- Post-vote `reveal` is server state for scoring + Next/Wrap consensus; the viral climax is the **finale scoreboard**, not per-round tallies.
- Original prompts only — never paste Kumple’s question bank.
- Preserve round/vote history when adding end/replay — needed for future Friend Profile (B-lite).

## SHOULD

- One vote per player per round (DB unique).
- Skip is always allowed on `challenge` / `truth` (no shame UX) when those kinds return.
- Tempo is **consensus intents**: lobby Ready (`continue`), post-reveal **Next** vs **Wrap up**, **all-voted → reveal**. Finale scoreboard on wrap / empty bank; Play again rotates `sessionKey`.
- Soft target ~8–12 rounds; UI may nudge wrap-up from round 8 — no hard stop.
- Sweet spot copy: 3–8 players in the channel.
